sudden|unexpectedly-quick|ADJECTIVE|happening quickly without warning|Happening quickly and without much warning.|đột ngột; bất ngờ|A sudden gust scattered the papers across the courtyard.|Một cơn gió bất chợt làm giấy tờ bay khắp sân.|Common before change, movement, or noise; all of a sudden is an adverbial phrase meaning unexpectedly.|0
warrior|fighter|NOUN|person known for fighting|A person who fights, especially in a war or in accounts of past battles.|chiến binh|The mural depicts a warrior returning to an empty village.|Bức tranh tường khắc họa một chiến binh trở về ngôi làng vắng người.|Countable; often historical or literary. A figurative warrior for a cause is a separate contextual use.|0
anybody|unspecified-person|PRONOUN|an unspecified person|Any person, without saying who that person is.|ai; bất kỳ ai|Has anybody seen the key to the rehearsal room?|Có ai thấy chìa khóa phòng tập không?|Normally takes a singular verb; common in questions, negatives, and conditions. Any adjective follows it, as in anybody interested.|0
anybody|free-choice-person|PRONOUN|any person without restriction|Any person, regardless of who they are.|bất cứ ai; ai cũng|Anybody can submit a drawing for the village calendar.|Bất cứ ai cũng có thể nộp một bức vẽ cho lịch của làng.|Used in affirmative statements for unrestricted choice; anybody can emphasizes that no particular identity is required.|0
firearm|gun|NOUN|gun that fires a projectile|A gun that uses an explosive charge to fire a projectile.|súng; vũ khí sử dụng thuốc phóng|The museum displayed an unloaded historic firearm behind glass.|Bảo tàng trưng bày một khẩu súng cổ không có đạn phía sau lớp kính.|Countable; firearm is a formal general term for a gun. It does not specify the type, permission to possess it, or a method of use.|0
lunch|midday-meal|NOUN|meal eaten around midday|A meal usually eaten around the middle of the day.|bữa trưa|They ate lunch on the covered terrace while the rain continued.|Họ ăn trưa trên hiên có mái che trong khi mưa vẫn tiếp diễn.|Usually uncountable in have lunch or after lunch; a lunch can name a particular meal or organized event.|0
